  "notes": "Zone and transfer points from 'Dieppe On-Demand Transit Service Zone.geojson' and 'Dieppe On-Demand Transit Transfer Points.geojson', sent by the City of Dieppe (Urban Mobility) to Atlas Outreach on 2026-10-16: the revised boundary in effect since Aug 23, 2026. Geometry used exactly as given (WGS84 in the file). The zone is the file's zone 1 (TAD 1.1 and TAD 1.2), drawn as one MultiPolygon; it matches the turquoise zone on the City's map. Left out: the 8 small zone-2 shapes (TAD 2.1 to 2.8), each drawn around one of the 8 transfer points, which are drawn as points instead; 'Zone_3_Airport' (designated stop 3020, 'Aeroport'), a 0.3 km2 box at YQM, was left out at first and added in CIV-1572 (2026-11-14), geometry as given, once the Greater Moncton airport's own page (cyqm.ca/to-from/transportation) confirmed Dieppe on-demand serves the airport. The 8 transfer points match the list on the City's page (2 main, 6 secondary). Hours from the City's page and FAQ; no holiday hours are stated. The service is free and open to everyone (children 11 and under ride with someone 12 or older). Pickup is at a stop the app assigns, usually under 500 m away (FAQ); no pickup method is set because the pickup line would count the transfer points as those stops. Booking: Blaise Transit app, ride.blaisetransit.com or 506-877-7818. Run by the City of Dieppe, not Codiac Transpo, so it is its own on-demand-only agency (the 'dieppe' slug is Dieppe, France)."
}
